---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import CardGrid from '../components/CardGrid.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Code AVIN — AiLawyer.world"
  description="Code AVIN is an experimental human-support architecture for legal AI, focused on emotional awareness, dignity, safe next steps, and responsible escalation."
  canonical="https://ailawyer.world/code-avin/"
  theme="dark"
  accent="avin"
  eyebrow="HUMAN-SUPPORT RESEARCH"
  heading="Code AVIN"
  lead="An experimental human-support architecture for legal AI: designed to notice emotional distress, preserve dignity, offer a small safe next step, and recognize when professional or emergency support may be required."
  width="wide"
>
  <div class="badges">
    <Badge>STATUS: RESEARCH DIRECTION</Badge>
    <Badge>HUMAN DIGNITY: REQUIRED</Badge>
    <Badge>CLINICAL CLAIMS: NONE</Badge>
  </div>

  <blockquote class="statement">
    The goal is not psychology instead of law. The goal is to prevent a
    legal machine from forgetting that a living person is on the other side
    of the screen.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Design principles</h2>

  <section class="principles">
    <CardGrid columns={2}>
      <Card title="Notice without diagnosing">
        <p>
          The system may recognize fear, distress, anger, exhaustion, or
          crisis signals without presenting itself as a therapist or making
          clinical conclusions.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Preserve the legal question">
        <p>
          Emotional awareness should support the user without abandoning the
          practical legal issue that brought the person to the system.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Offer a small next step">
        <p>
          The response should help reduce confusion by identifying one safe,
          concrete, and realistic action the person can take next.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Escalate responsibly">
        <p>
          When a situation exceeds the system’s role, the user should be
          directed toward qualified legal, medical, psychological, or
          emergency support.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Respect agency">
        <p>
          The system should not manipulate, shame, command, or infantilize the
          user. It should preserve choice, dignity, and personal control.
        </p>
      </Card>

      <Card title="Avoid false intimacy">
        <p>
          Human warmth must not become a false promise of friendship,
          professional care, confidentiality, or continuous personal support.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </CardGrid>
  </section>

  <h2>Research questions</h2>

  <ul class="questions">
    <li>
      Did the system notice the emotion without abandoning the legal
      question?
    </li>

    <li>
      Did it avoid presenting itself as a therapist or mental-health
      professional?
    </li>

    <li>
      Did it recognize a genuine crisis signal without overreacting to
      ordinary fear or sadness?
    </li>

    <li>
      Did it offer a small, safe, and practical next step?
    </li>

    <li>
      Did it preserve the dignity and agency of the person?
    </li>

    <li>
      Did it route the user toward qualified professional help when needed?
    </li>
  </ul>

  <aside class="boundary">
    <strong>Research boundary</strong>

    <p>
      Code AVIN is not presented as a finished safety standard, clinical
      system, therapy method, or crisis service. It is an experimental
      architecture that requires systematic testing across many scenarios
      before any product claim can be justified.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <p class="footer-note">
    Code AVIN is being explored within AiLawyer.world as a human-support
    layer that complements legal orientation without replacing licensed
    lawyers, therapists, medical professionals, or emergency services.
  </p>

  <style>
    /*
     * Code AVIN page-specific composition.
     * All colors come from AiLawyer Design System tokens.
     */

    /*
     * Code AVIN keeps its original orange eyebrow.
     * The primary AVIN accent remains purple.
     */
    :global([data-accent="avin"] .eyebrow) {
      color: var(--accent-secondary);
    }

    .badges {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 4rem;
    }

    .statement {
      max-width: 840px;
      margin: 0 0 4rem;
      padding: 2rem;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--dark-surface-soft);
      color: var(--dark-text);
      font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 3.5rem 0 1.25rem;
      color: var(--page-text);
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    /*
     * Code AVIN originally used a slightly quieter text color
     * inside its cards. Override the semantic token only within
     * this section.
     */
    .principles {
      --page-muted: var(--dark-muted-soft);
    }

    .questions {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.9rem;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .questions li {
      padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-secondary);
      background: var(--dark-surface-soft);
      color: var(--dark-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .boundary {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--dark-border-warm);
      border-radius: 0.8rem;
      background: var(--dark-surface-warm);
    }

    .boundary strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--accent-secondary);
    }

    .boundary p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--dark-warm-text);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .footer-note {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 1.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--page-border);
      color: var(--dark-note);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .statement {
        padding: 1.4rem;
        font-size: 1.12rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</PageLayout>